                        "glosses": [
                            "An act of shoogling; a shake."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8576bd5-21a9-442b-9d57-026dd92582a2",
                                "sense_id": "2267920a-406d-3906-a460-2dc468c3db17",
                                "text": "First and foremost, howsever, gie that sleepy body, Dirdumwhamle, a shoogle out o' his dreams."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd1896b4-7472-4728-a3b5-be0e5c8260bc",
                                "sense_id": "2267920a-406d-3906-a460-2dc468c3db17",
                                "text": "To him, it might as well have been music, and his subsequent display of dance kicks and bum shoogles, had them all in hysterics."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19f41368-c957-40bf-9a42-2ecc98e51378",
                                "sense_id": "2267920a-406d-3906-a460-2dc468c3db17",
                                "text": "And when he would be sayin' good-bye to them from the brudge, he would chust take off his hat and give it a shoogle, and put it on again; his manners wass complete."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
